<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Criccieth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Criccieth is a small town on Tremadog Bay in Gwynedd, north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, in the old district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eifionydd">Eifionydd</a>. Its castle was built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a> in the 1230s and was taken and strengthened by Edward I after his conquest of Wales in 1283. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a>'s forces captured and burned it in 1404.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/criccieth.jpg" alt="Criccieth" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James@hopgrove at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Criccieth_beach.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
